(lang dune 3.13)

; Strict-warning profile, used by the advisory CI job.
;
; The root dune file deliberately leaves -warn-error off for normal builds: the
; C++ stub layer cannot avoid a few warnings, and promoting them to errors there
; would only get in the way. This profile turns them into errors on demand,
; without changing what a plain `dune build` does.
;
; dune 3 removed the `--flags` command-line option, and a (profile ...) stanza
; cannot carry flags either, so the supported way to inject compiler flags for a
; named profile is an env stanza keyed by that profile's name.
;
; Known to fail today, which is why the CI job is continue-on-error. The warning
; set matches the root dune file's, minus `-warn-error -a`.
(env
 (warnings
  (flags
   (:standard -w +a-4-9-40-41-42-44-45-48-70 -warn-error +a))))